      "a": "The heats released in the two reactions are not equal. The heat released in a reaction depends on the reactants, products and the physical states.\nIn reaction:\nWater is produced in the gaseous state whereas in\nIt is in liquid state.\nAlso, when water vapors condensed to form water latent heat of vaporization is released. Therefore, more heat is released in reaction (ii)."
